## 1. Introduction and Purpose

This document outlines the commercial pricing structure for the MedSync Health platform, detailing the three primary subscription tiers: Standard, Professional, and Enterprise. The purpose of this document is to provide a framework for the Sales and Finance teams to generate quotes, ensuring consistency in feature allocation and service level agreements (SLAs) across all customer segments.

The pricing model is designed to align with the value delivered to our core customer base—hospitals, clinics, and insurance providers—reflecting the complexity and scale of the digital health solutions deployed. Our strong Net Revenue Retention (NRR) of **118%** [1] and high Logo Retention Rate of **87%** [1] underscore the long-term value proposition embedded in these tiers.

---

## 2. MedSync Core Pricing Tiers

MedSync Health employs a value-based pricing strategy, with tiers structured around the depth of integration, volume of data processing, and required compliance features. The following table details the base monthly subscription rates.

| Tier | Base Monthly Rate (AED) | Notes on Ambiguity and Negotiation |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Standard** | **AED 2,940/month** | Target: AED 2,205, Enterprise: AED 3,675. *Reflects a base rate for smaller clinics or single-product deployments.* |
| **Professional** | **AED 7,350/month** | Target: AED 5,512.50, Enterprise: AED 9,187.50. *Intended for multi-product deployments with mid-level data volume requirements.* |
| **Enterprise** | **AED 14,700/month** | Target: AED 11,025, Enterprise: AED 18,375. *Reserved for large hospital systems, reflecting the Average Contract Value (ACV) for Hospitals of **AED 735,000** annually [1].* |

**Note on Ambiguity:** The pricing structure intentionally includes a range of potential rates (Target, Enterprise) to accommodate regional market variations, competitive pressures, and volume discounts. The "Base Monthly Rate" serves as the list price, while the "Target" and "Enterprise" figures represent the lower bound for high-volume, multi-year contracts and the upper bound for highly customized, premium service agreements, respectively.

